{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BntMRveGsJRUqpy9HLYrMc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full paper and the review context. Let me now dispatch two reviewers in parallel:\n\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n\nI'll launch them as parallel agents, then do the roundtable synthesis myself.\n\nLet me carefully structure the review. The paper is:\n\n**Title**: OntoCoDec: Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\n\n**Summary**: Proposes OntoCoDec, a two-layer constrained decoding framework for structured IE that compiles ontology schemas into (1) a grammar layer (CFG via XGrammar for type vocabulary constraints) and (2) a semantic layer (stateful entity registry for context-sensitive domain/range constraints). \n\nThe evaluation spans relation and event extraction tasks across multiple model sizes and both zero-shot and fine-tuned settings. Now I'll set up the parallel reviewers to analyze the methods and experimental results on one track, while examining the novelty and positioning relative to existing work on the other.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15620,"cache_read_input_tokens":45007,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15620},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5cda2c76-b1bb-4b5e-b780-c4d3c1c78b32","uuid":"337b523a-374d-4083-987b-073eba798c4a"}
